"""
RADIANT - build hook (pure Python: the builder runs it with the system python3).

Generates radiant_pkg.vhd from data measured on duci.jpg (a paper collage; working files in
.heirloom_work/rb_radiant/: masks, zone polygons, tables2.py, zones_ref.py, gen_hook.py).

  C_TAB    1024 x 16: the four cut-outs (0 hands, 1 bust, 2 woman, 3 soldier) as slot tables.
           Address = figure(2) & row(6) & word(2).  64 rows over each figure's height; per row six
           monotone edges (8-bit, units of 2 virtual px from the figure's left) and five zone labels
           (3 bits, local zone index, 7 = transparent): w0 = e1:e0, w1 = e3:e2, w2 = e5:e4,
           w3 = lerp(15) & z4..z0.  lerp = 1: the edges interpolate towards row r+1.
  C_PALY / C_PALC  256 x 16: the zone ramps.  Address = zone(4) & level(4); each zone's 16 entries are
           the mean colours of its 16 luma quantiles on the collage (hardware convention u = Cr,
           v = Cb).  C_PALY = {DUCI(5:0), Y}; C_PALC = {U(9:2), V(9:2)}.  The spare top bits of
           C_PALY hold the DUCI label: a 60 x 24 bitmap, word row * 10 + group = 6 columns (bit 0 left).
  C_LENS   256 x 16 (block RAM; 64 words used): the glasses' lens half widths (half virtual px) per row over page
           y 912..1030: word 2r = {left outer, left inner}, 2r+1 = {right outer, right inner}, 8 bits each.
  C_OVH / C_OVL  256 x 16 (block RAM): every drawn colour: 0..127 ground (level(2) & luma multiplier
           x/16 (5)), 128.. coffee ramp, 144.. cup wall shades, 160 + k flat colours (rays, halo, ring,
           gold, rim, frame, eye, flag).  {Y, U(9:4)} / {U(3:0), V, "00"}.
"""
